Subject: [PATCH] disable unsupported shared memory io plugin on Android

On Android 14+ (Bionic libc), POSIX shm_open() is absent, ashmem is
deprecated and removed from NDK headers and Linux 5.18+ kernels, and
System V IPC (shmat/shmdt) is disallowed by Android SELinux policies and
disabled in default Android kernels (CONFIG_SYSVIPC=n).

Disable the implementation on __ANDROID__ so librz/io falls back to
the clean stub plugin descriptor.

--- a/librz/io/p/io_shm.c
+++ b/librz/io/p/io_shm.c
@@ -9,3 +9,3 @@
 
-#if HAVE_HEADER_LINUX_ASHMEM_H || HAVE_HEADER_SYS_SHM_H || __WINDOWS__
+#if (HAVE_HEADER_LINUX_ASHMEM_H || HAVE_HEADER_SYS_SHM_H || __WINDOWS__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)
 #if HAVE_HEADER_LINUX_ASHMEM_H
